# SM-T715 (Galaxy Tab S2 8.0 LTE, arm64 port) build of omamobile's
# omamobile-shell 0.2.147 for Omarchy 4.5, after the owner's other tablet port
# (Lenovomarchy, image/pkg/omamobile-shell 0.2.133-3, which runs on its tablet
# over Omarchy 4.5.0-3) with the SM-T715's own tablet patches carried forward
# from its 0.2.94/0.2.133 builds.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/derekross/omamobile, packages/
# omamobile-shell 0.2.147 at commit 899184543d60fd78f0a418f403463d628165a3ed,
# tarball checked by sha256 (top directory omamobile-<commit>).
#
# What it is: ordinary Omarchy shell plugins (QML) that turn Omarchy's shell
# into a touch shell: a status bar with a pull-down quick-settings sheet
# (omamobile.bar replaces omarchy.bar), the dock, app drawer and search bar
# (omamobile.launcher), recent apps (omamobile.switcher), home screens
# (omamobile.home, built-in widgets only), the call card (omamobile.call),
# the keyboard's show/hide calls and language sheet (omamobile.keyboard),
# the edge back swipe (omamobile.back) and the voice bar (omamobile.voice:
# speech to text through Voxtype, in the session's language);
# omamobile-setup-user links them into the user's config. Nothing here is
# compiled and nothing patches Hyprland (the image's rootfs/t715-tablet.lua
# has the window rules; upstream's hypr/phone.lua is not installed).
#
# The series (this directory; each patch's header says more):
#   0001 tablet-quick-settings-tiles  no torch, location, NFC or fingerprint
#        tiles (Mobile data comes back in 0010); Hotspot under "Add tiles";
#        Rotation in the default layout (Lenovomarchy's 0001, with the
#        SM-T715's tiles)
#   0002 tablet-wifi-wpa2-without-sae  WPA2-PSK for a WPA3/WPA2 SSID: the
#        BCM4358 firmware has no SAE (Lenovomarchy's 0002; the SM-T715's 0002)
#   0003 tablet-quiet-pollers  no do-not-disturb poll; the modem and call
#        watchers only when the profile asks (true in tablet-shell.json;
#        rebased on 0.2.147's bar.statusIcons.cell/showCell; Lenovomarchy's 0003)
#   0004 tablet-phone-leftovers  no unshipped plugin, menu row or probe
#        (Lenovomarchy's 0004), with upstream's suspend-off step kept and its
#        tile-refresh guard fixed for the Rotation tile this build keeps;
#        omamobile.call is shipped again (the modem runs on arm64 now), and
#        omamobile.voice too, with Setup > Voice and the Voxtype setup
#   0005 tablet-rotate-tile  Rotate: a quarter turn by hand (t715-rotate)
#   0006 tablet-airplane-and-hotspot  Airplane mode through nmcli radio for
#        Wi-Fi and the modem; Hotspot shows its password (stray .orig hunk dropped)
#   0007 tablet-set-pin  "tablet" wording; sudo asks once a PIN is set (rebased
#        onto 0.2.147's --change/PTY PIN helper)
#   0008 tablet-back-gesture  the swipe is the Back key's (t715-keys), with
#        upstream's Escape as the fallback
#   0009 tablet-sdcard-tile  the SD card tile over t715-sdcard
#   0010 tablet-modem  the Mobile data tile back, through NetworkManager's
#        gsm connection (t715-mobile); signal bars and technology from
#        shannonctl status (the SM-T715's 0.2.94 series' 0004)
#   0011 tablet-mobile-settings  the Mobile data tile's long press, or a tap
#        while no connection exists, opens t715-mobile-settings (the 0.2.94
#        series' 0006)
#   0012 tablet-modem-tile  the Modem tile over t715-modem-power; the Mobile
#        data tile says "Modem off" while it is off (the 0.2.94 series' 0011)
#   0013 tablet-call-card  no Speaker toggle on the call card (no earpiece;
#        the 0.2.94 series' 0007's call-card hunk)
#   0014 tablet-voice-language  the voice bar in other languages than
#        English: a Language choice in the voice settings (Automatic and
#        seven languages, Voxtype's [whisper] language), the models
#        following it (.en for English, the multilingual tiny/base/small
#        otherwise), the live preview in that language, and Voxtype set up
#        out of the box with ggml-base.bin or ggml-base.en.bin, in the
#        session's language (the tablet's omamobile-voice, pkg-voice, ships
#        the multilingual base)
#   0015 tablet-onboarding  bin/omamobile-onboarding ships, adapted to the
#        tablet: the image's placeholder password (0007 names it) counts as
#        no PIN, so the login nudge asks for setup and --inner makes the user
#        choose a PIN or password; the modem line over shannond (shannonctl
#        status, t715-modem-power for the modem's own switch; the APN is set
#        in Réseau mobile, the Modem tile switches the modem on); Golden's
#        AI step in --inner (the AI desktop apps in one multi-choice, the
#        voice-input language, the default coding agent). The image starts
#        the nudge itself (omamobile-onboarding --nudge at login; hypr/
#        phone.lua, which does it on the phone, is not installed from here)
#   0016 tablet-android-tile  the Android tile over t715-android (the
#        0.2.94 series' 0013, ported): on while the Waydroid session runs,
#        "Asleep" while the container is frozen; a tap starts or stops the
#        session, a long press opens Android Settings; dimmed when Waydroid
#        is not installed
# Not carried forward from the SM-T715's 0.2.94 series, for the arm64 image
# (the commands they drive are not in it): 0010 tablet-location-tile (no
# t715-gps). Upstream did what the 0.2.94 series' 0009 worked around (Escape
# by name): 0008 keeps upstream's fix as its fallback.
#
# The profiles: profile/shell.json is tablet-shell.json (only the plugins
# shipped here, the call card and the voice bar among them, the drawer at 6
# columns, Omarchy's idle timers at 0 (off; t715-idle turns the screen off),
# the modem and call watchers on (the modem runs on arm64 now), the 18
# bar-widget-only Omarchy plugins and omarchy.remote-session in
# disabledPlugins; omarchy.idle stays, as on the 0.2.94 build) and
# profile/home.json is tablet-home.json (Lenovomarchy's 6x8 home grid with
# the image's apps).
#
# Shipped from 0.2.147's new pieces: bin/omamobile-browser-setup (replaces the
# inline Chromium/Grok Bot steps in omamobile-setup-user and is invoked by
# omamobile.bar's Bar.qml at shell start; Python stdlib only) and
# plugins/omamobile.bar/BatteryIndicator.qml (installed with omamobile.bar).
# Shipped again since 0.2.147-2.1: the voice bar (plugins/omamobile.voice,
# bin/omamobile-voice for the Dictation tile and scripts,
# bin/omamobile-voice-preview for its live words), which Lenovomarchy's
# build and this one's 0.2.147-1.1 left out, with 0014 for the tablet's
# French session. Voxtype (voxtype-bin) and the model (omamobile-voice, the
# tablet's build in pkg-voice: Whisper's multilingual base) stay optional,
# as upstream has them; without Voxtype the voice settings say so. The ways
# in from here: a hold on the home pill and the Dictation tile (under "Add
# tiles", 0001); the keyboard's Mic key is the image's to bind (upstream's
# squeekboard layouts and hypr/phone.lua are not installed from here).
# Dropped from upstream's install, as Lenovomarchy drops them (its PKGBUILD
# has every reason): the plugins omamobile.fingerprint, .update, .access,
# .mobilenetwork; the bins for fingerprint enrolment, NFC, the
# phone's keys, sleep and double-tap daemons, the permission
# portal, intents, weather, mobile network and the update sheet's
# reboot; hypr/phone.lua, squeekboard's layouts (including 0.2.147's Greek
# terminal layouts) and their generator (the image ships its own terminal
# layouts with Esc), the keyboard theme hook, the OSK and fcitx5 environment
# files, the portal drop-ins, the desktop entries and omamobile-osk-guard.
# bin/omamobile-onboarding ships (0015, adapted to the tablet); the image
# starts its --nudge at login itself, as hypr/phone.lua does on the phone
# (that file is not installed from here). Not
# depended on: omamobile-apps (the dialer, SMS, NFC and maps),
# omamobile-omarchy (the image installs it anyway), omamobile-owl-widgets
# (off), omatel-agent (the image keeps it; the call plugin and both watchers
# ship again, 0004 and 0013).
#
# Build: tools/build-pkg omamobile-shell (rootfs/build.sh does it). Image:
# rootfs/install-mobile.sh, rootfs/omarchy-user-setup.sh; checks: the smoke
# check.

# Maintainer (upstream): Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>

pkgname=omamobile-shell
pkgver=0.2.147
pkgrel=3.2
pkgdesc="Omamobile's touch shell for Omarchy: status bar, quick settings, launcher, recents, home, back swipe, voice bar (SM-T715 tablet build)"
arch=(any)
url="https://github.com/derekross/omamobile"
license=(MIT)
depends=(
  'omarchy>=4.0.6'
  bash python python-dbus python-gobject   # osk-watch, bt-agent, keyboard-languages, widget
  squeekboard                               # the on-screen keyboard (sm.puri.OSK0)
  quickshell                                # the host shell (qs); pulled by omarchy already
  qt6-declarative                           # the QML runtime the plugins import
  bluez bluez-utils                         # Bluetooth panel and rfkill
  networkmanager iw                         # Wi-Fi panel, the SAE probe (patch 0002)
  util-linux                                # busctl (keyboard tile), rfkill
  jq                                        # BackModel's terminal sniff, omamobile-launch
  inotify-tools                             # the home screen's user-widget watch
  wtype                                     # the back gesture's Escape (its fallback here); voice typing
  which                                     # voice: Voxtype finds wtype and wl-copy with it
  wf-recorder                               # the Screen record tile
  libnotify                                 # omamobile-screenrecord's fallback toast
  brightnessctl                             # the brightness slider
  gum                                       # omamobile-onboarding's and omamobile-set-pin's prompts
)
optdepends=(
  'loupe: what a screenshot toast opens (omamobile-screenshot-open); the image installs it'
  'khal: events in the home screen calendar widget'
  'playerctl: the home screen media widget'
  'power-profiles-daemon: the Battery saver tile (dimmed "No power profiles" without it)'
  'hyprsunset: the Night light tile (dimmed "No hyprsunset" without it)'
  "omamobile-settings: Omarchy Mobile's Settings app (independent of the shell; the image installs it)"
  'foot: a terminal for omamobile-launch cmd and the agent prompt (any xdg-terminal-exec works)'
  'voxtype-bin: the voice bar (speech to text; or Install > AI > Dictation)'
  "omamobile-voice: Whisper's model for Voxtype, voice with no download (the tablet's: multilingual base)"
)
checkdepends=(nodejs diffutils patch python python-dbus python-gobject jq util-linux)
install=omamobile-shell.install

_commit=899184543d60fd78f0a418f403463d628165a3ed
_tarball="omamobile-${_commit:0:7}.tar.gz"
_dir="omamobile-${_commit}/packages/omamobile-shell"
_patches=(
